{
  "schema": 1,
  "kind": "behavioural",
  "machine": "records",
  "name": "records_a_tampered_body_is_rejected_and_not_gossiped_onward",
  "description": "The mesh key is symmetric and shared, so any paired device can put bytes on the wire that are authentic at the transport layer. Per-record signing is what stops a compromised renderer rewriting a zone. A record that fails is dropped rather than held, because gossiping it onward would spread the forgery at the speed of the replication protocol.",
